+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/closing-costs/#article","headline":"South Carolina Closing Costs Calculator: Buyers Pay 2-5%","description":"A South Carolina closing costs calculator for buyers and sellers, with the real line items: the $1.85-per-$500 deed recording fee, attorney-state closing fees, title insurance rates, Horry County's in-arrears tax escrows, VA fee rules, and typical totals.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/closing-costs/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-07-20","dateModified":"2026-11-07","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/closing-costs/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"South Carolina closing costs"},"keywords":"closing costs South Carolina, SC closing costs calculator, how much are closing costs in SC, who pays closing costs South Carolina, SC deed stamps"}</script>
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/closing-costs/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are closing costs in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Buyers typically pay roughly 2 to 5 percent of the price in closing costs and prepaids, covering lender fees, the attorney, title insurance, and escrow deposits. Benchmark surveys put the third-party-plus-tax portion near $2,900 on an average South Carolina purchase, before lender fees and prepaids. Sellers pay the commission they negotiate plus about 0.37 percent in deed stamps and small document fees."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the transfer tax in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The seller, by statute. South Carolina's deed recording fee is $1.85 per $500 of price, which is $1,480 on a $400,000 sale, and state law makes it the grantor's liability. It is often called deed stamps or transfer tax; the money splits $1.30 to the state and $0.55 to the county."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an attorney to close on a house in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The South Carolina Supreme Court requires a licensed attorney to supervise real estate closings, including the title work, document preparation, recording, and disbursement. Residential closing fees typically run $600 to $1,200, and the buyer customarily selects and pays the closing attorney."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a CL-100 letter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"South Carolina's official wood infestation report, covering termites and wood-destroying organisms. Most lenders require one, it typically costs about $75 to $150, and it is ordered near closing because it is valid for roughly 45 days. Homes with crawl spaces are the ones to watch."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is my Horry County tax escrow so high?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two reasons. Taxes here are billed in arrears, mailed October 1 and due January 15, so the lender collects months of them up front. If the home will not be your legal residence, it is assessed at the 6 percent ratio with the full school operating tax, several times the seller's 4 percent bill. A correct escrow is built on your future bill, not the seller's old one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the VA funding fee in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A one-time percentage of the loan that varies with first or subsequent VA use and with any down payment you choose to make; more down means a smaller fee. Veterans receiving service-connected disability compensation are exempt. The fee is almost always financed into the loan rather than paid in cash."}}]}</script>
