 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the latest NFIP reauthorization update?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Federal flood insurance runs until Dec. 11 under the stopgap spending law signed on Sept. 2. Congress must extend it by then, or FEMA cannot sell new flood policies until it does."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to my flood insurance if the program lapses on Dec. 11?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your current policy stays in force to the end of its one-year term, and FEMA keeps paying claims. FEMA cannot sell new policies until Congress acts. A buyer who needs a new policy waits or uses private flood insurance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will Annie Andrews vote on the Dec. 11 flood insurance deadline?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The new Senate term starts Jan. 3, after the deadline. Sen. Darline Graham holds the seat until then. Andrews votes on any extension or flood bill after she takes office."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a home closing happen during a flood insurance lapse?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with a private flood policy the lender accepts. Some lenders also waived the requirement in the lapse that ran from October to November 2025. In the June 2010 lapse, an estimated 1,400 closings a day were canceled or delayed nationwide."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can the governor of South Carolina change flood insurance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Only Congress can change federal flood insurance. Alan Wilson's insurance item, as reported, is about state audits of rate increases, with yearly public reports from major carriers."}}]}</script>
