 ## Why does a second home or rental in Myrtle Beach pay more property tax?
-A home you do not live in pays more for two reasons. The state constitution taxes it on 6% of its value instead of 4%, and it still pays the school operating tax.
-
-- The 4% rate is for the home you live in and up to five acres around it. You apply to the county for it. Without the application, the home is taxed at 6%.
-
-- The 6% rate is for all other real property: a second home, a rental, a lot, or a shop.
-
+The state constitution taxes a home you do not live in on 6% of its value instead of 4%, and it still pays the school operating tax. On the same house inside Myrtle Beach, that makes the second-home bill more than twice the homeowner's. Our Horry County property tax guide shows how each bill is figured, and our page for rental investors works each bill at 6% and 4% .
