+## What are the short-term rental rules in each town today?
+Each town writes its own rules today. Our short-term rental rules guide lists them town by town, with every license and tax. The short version follows.
 
-- Residential zones. No zone that begins with R allows them, except RMV (Residential Multifamily Visitor). Most traditional neighborhoods are in R zones.
+- Myrtle Beach keeps short-term rentals, stays of under 90 days, out of most of its residential neighborhoods. No zone that begins with R allows them, except RMV. Fewer than 30 houses in those zones can keep renting under the old rules.
 
-- Grandfathered houses. Fewer than 30 houses in those zones, citywide, can keep renting short-term under the old rules.
+- North Myrtle Beach allows them with a city business license , renewed every year, and no special zoning.
 
-- License and fines. Every rental needs a city business license. A violation can bring a fine of up to $500, 30 days in jail, or both, on conviction.
+- Surfside Beach and Horry County outside the cities each decide their own rules too.
 
